      "patch": "@@ -20,6 +20,9 @@ principal ideal generated by `Abar - 1`. Following the PDF, we first prove this\n relation irreducible by scaling weighted homogeneous components, then compare\n prime ideals in the two-dimensional polynomial ring.\n \n+Consequently, `rAlgebraEquivQuotient` presents the algebra of reduced level-one\n+Fourier expansions as the polynomial algebra modulo `Abar - 1`.\n+\n The scaling argument is adapted from `AbarSubOne.lean` in\n `PartitionsLeanblueprint.RamanujanCongruence.AiAssisted.SwD`.\n -/\n@@ -878,6 +881,21 @@ theorem hasseIdeal_eq_span : hasseIdeal p = Ideal.span {Abar p - 1} := by\n   have : (3 : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ 2 := hheight3'.trans (hMdim.trans hdim)\n   norm_num at this\n \n+/-- The algebra of modular forms modulo `p`, identified by their Fourier expansions,\n+is the polynomial algebra in the reduced Eisenstein series modulo `Abar - 1`. -/\n+def rAlgebraEquiv :\n+    ModularFormMod.rAlgebra (PInteger.reduce (p := p)) 𝒮ℒ ≃ₐ[ZMod p]\n+      MvPolynomial (Fin 2) (ZMod p) ⧸ Ideal.span {Abar p - 1} :=\n+  (ModularFormMod.eisensteinFourierQuotientEquiv (PInteger.reduce (p := p))).symm.trans\n+    (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq (ZMod p) (hasseIdeal_eq_span p))\n+\n+/-- The inverse quotient presentation evaluates a polynomial at the reduced Fourier\n+expansions of `E₄` and `E₆`. -/\n+@[simp] theorem coe_rAlgebraEquiv_symm_mk (F : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) (ZMod p)) :\n+    ((rAlgebraEquiv p).symm\n+      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {Abar p - 1}) F) : PowerSeries (ZMod p)) =\n+      ModularFormMod.eisensteinFourierEval (PInteger.reduce (p := p)) F := rfl\n+\n /-- The same generator in the existing graded Hasse ideal, via Eisenstein evaluation. -/\n theorem graded_hasseIdeal_eq_span :\n     ModularFormMod.hasseIdeal (Γ := 𝒮ℒ) (PInteger.reduce (p := p)) ="
